                            MEDITATION ON PROSPERITY

Preface

Josh.1:8 says, ‘Do not let this book of the law depart
from your mouth; meditate on it day and night, so that
you may be careful to do everything written in it. Then
you will be prosperous and successful’ (NIV).

This scripture shows the direct relationship between
meditation of scriptures and obedience to the principles
of God’s word in engendering prosperity.

The word translated ‘meditate’ in scripture denotes ‘to
speak’, ‘utter’, and even ‘shout’. Thus, these meditations
are to be said loudly and not merely to be skimmed with
the eye. As you declare these scriptures prophetically
into your life, you are creating prosperous events,
conditions and a bright future for yourself by the power
of the Word that created the universe.

It may take time for the things of the spirit to materalise
in the physical, so it is important that you engage these
meditations routinely and consistently. Kindly find a
suitable environment where you can effectively and
prayerfully confess these meditations and watch as the
‘harvest of prosperity begin to accrue in your life.
